        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "improve: enforce canonical QA scenario ownership",
        "body": "Closes #99627\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a QA maintenance problem where scenario IDs could be owned by both the canonical YAML inventory and a code-defined live transport catalog without one validation failure identifying both owners. It also prevents helper-level or in-memory tests from being presented as primary evidence for coverage that requires a real product boundary executable.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe existing `qa coverage` path now records one owner for every YAML flow, script, Vitest, and Playwright scenario plus every remaining Discord, Slack, Telegram, and WhatsApp live scenario. Coverage generation rejects duplicate IDs with both source references, reports the remaining legacy owner count, and keeps helper-backed claims under supporting `coverage.secondary` metadata. The existing live transport CLI commands remain mounted on the shared `openclaw qa` host.\n\nLegacy catalog and compatibility-wrapper deletion criteria are documented so migrations can remove old owners only after canonical YAML execution and evidence parity are established.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThere is no end-user runtime behavior change. QA maintainers and contributors get deterministic duplicate-ID failures, explicit ownership in machine-readable coverage output, and more accurate scorecard evidence semantics.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/qa-lab/src/coverage-report.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/scenario-catalog.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/scenario-packs.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/live-transports/shared/live-transport-scenarios.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/cli.test.ts extensions/qa-lab/src/cli.runtime.test.ts` — 223 tests passed.\n- Follow-up catalog/pack rerun — 55 tests passed.\n- `node --import tsx scripts/qa-coverage-report.ts --json` — 155 YAML scenarios plus 82 live catalog scenarios produced 237 unique owner IDs.\n- `node scripts/format-docs.mjs --check docs/concepts/qa-e2e-automation.md qa/README.md` — passed.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kwmne1hs8mxq54avrspedbmc` — `corepack pnpm check:changed` passed, including project typecheck, lint, guards, and runtime import-cycle validation.\n- Codex autoreview — no accepted/actionable findings, confidence 0.93.\n",
